  "authoringNote": "Under C01, 2026-02-10 plus six calendar months is 2026-08-10 (day 10 exists in August, no clamping) and the inclusive bound is that date. The final order is dated 2026-09-02, 23 days after the bound, so the encounter and order pair holds R04.order_after_bound, a conflict for the administrative reviewer (SPEC R04 and F05: chronology conflict, never ready). The order follows the encounter, so order_before_encounter does not hold, and both state SYN-PRAC-0001. All dates are valid ISO dates, so this is an R04 finding, not an input rejection. R04 cites status, date and practitioner identifier of both documents (six) and names no parent (C07). The receipt references the order and follows its date span (C06), so R05 passes. R01, R02, R03, R07, R08 and R09 pass, R06 is qualified clinical review with five clinical citations and no administrative effect, and R10 is not applicable. The state is needs_human_review.",
